# d24 — The mixed gauntlet (drill set)

The last set. Every problem here is two or three of the track's ideas at once,
and none of them announces which — that is the whole exercise. A controlled
input whose validity is derived; a list whose order is derived; a timer that
has to restart and a callback that has to be current; a context feeding a
request that can be overtaken; a hook with a reducer inside it; a queue where
every item has its own clock; a debounce that still needs a race guard; a
compound component that also has to manage focus.

The instruments are the ones used all the way through Volume 2: requests are
injected and resolved by hand, anything timed uses fake timers with
`fireEvent`, and every assertion is about something a user could see, hear, or
tab to.

If a problem stalls, the honest move is to name the ideas in it before writing
anything — the reading notes for this set are written the same way.

## Exercise 1 — the code, not the keystrokes

Edit `ex1/solution.tsx`. `VoucherBox({ onRedeem })` renders an input labelled
`Voucher` showing exactly what was typed, a `role="status"` paragraph reading
`Ready` or `Keep typing`, and a `Redeem` button. The **code** is the typed
value trimmed and upper-cased; it is ready at five characters or more, and that
is what `Redeem` sends.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex1
```

## Exercise 2 — one lead at a time

Edit `ex2/solution.tsx`. `RosterBoard({ people })` renders one `<li>` per
person containing their name — with ` (lead)` appended for the lead — and a
button reading `Promote <name>`. The lead is shown first and everybody else
keeps the order they arrived in; promoting somebody else moves the title; a
`Reset` button clears it. An empty roster renders `Nobody on the roster` in a
`role="status"` paragraph and no list.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex2
```

## Exercise 3 — the clock that restarts

Edit `ex3/solution.tsx`. `IdleWatcher({ timeoutMs, onIdle })` renders
`Active` or `Idle` in a `role="status"` paragraph and an `Activity` button.
`timeoutMs` after the last activity — not after mounting — it goes idle and
calls `onIdle` once. It uses whichever `onIdle` it has at that moment, and it
leaves no timer running once it is idle or once it is gone.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex3
```

## Exercise 4 — the profile for this session

Edit `ex4/solution.tsx`. `SessionProvider({ userId, children })` publishes the
current user id. `ProfilePane({ loadProfile })` takes **no** id as a prop: it
reads it from the session, calls `loadProfile(userId)`, shows
`Loading profile` in a `role="status"` paragraph until the answer arrives and
the name in a level-2 heading afterwards. When the session changes, the answer
to the old one must change nothing, whenever it turns up.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex4
```

## Exercise 5 — the cart is the hook

Edit `ex5/solution.tsx`. `useCart()` returns `{ lines, total, add, remove }`,
with a reducer inside it: `add` raises an existing line's quantity or starts a
new one, `remove` lowers it and drops the line at zero, `total` is the sum of
price times quantity, and `add` and `remove` are the same functions for the
life of the hook. `CartPanel({ products })` is only the markup — `Add <name>`
buttons, `<name> x<qty>` in `<li>`s, and `Total: <n>` in a `role="status"`
paragraph.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex5
```

## Exercise 6 — every toast on its own clock

Edit `ex6/solution.tsx`. `ToastQueue({ autoDismissMs })` renders a `Notify`
button which adds a toast reading `Message <n>`, numbered from 1 and never
reusing a number, each with a `Dismiss <message>` button. A toast disappears
`autoDismissMs` after **it** appeared — not after the queue last changed — and
dismissing one by hand or leaving the page cancels its timer.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex6
```

## Exercise 7 — quiet, then ask

Edit `ex7/solution.tsx`. `SearchWorkbench({ search })` renders an input
labelled `Query`, a `role="status"` paragraph reading `Idle`, `Searching` or
`<n> results`, and the results as `<li>`s. `search(query)` is called 300ms
after the **last** keystroke and not before — and the answer to a query the
user has moved on from must never reach the screen.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex7
```

## Exercise 8 — one step at a time

Edit `ex8/solution.tsx`. `Wizard` with `Wizard.Step({ title, children })` and
`Wizard.Nav()`. Only the current step is rendered, its `title` as a level-2
heading. `Nav` renders `Step <n> of <total>` in a `role="status"` paragraph and
`Back` and `Next` buttons, each disabled at its end — and it is never told the
step or the total by the caller. When the step changes, focus moves to the new
step's heading.

```
uv run dojo test react d24_mixed_gauntlet ex8
```

## The gate

This is the entire gate, `gate.test.tsx`:

<!-- GATE:BEGIN -->

```tsx
// Gate for react/d24_mixed_gauntlet. Quoted verbatim in README.md.
//
// The last set: every exercise is two or three of the track's ideas at once.
// The instruments are the same ones used all the way through - injected
// fetchers resolved by hand, fake timers with fireEvent, onRender spies, and
// assertions only about what a user could see or hear.
import { act, fireEvent, render, renderHook, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import { afterEach, describe, expect, test, vi } from "vitest";

import { VoucherBox } from "./ex1/solution";
import { RosterBoard } from "./ex2/solution";
import { IdleWatcher } from "./ex3/solution";
import { SessionProvider, ProfilePane } from "./ex4/solution";
import { useCart, CartPanel } from "./ex5/solution";
import { ToastQueue } from "./ex6/solution";
import { SearchWorkbench } from "./ex7/solution";
import { Wizard } from "./ex8/solution";

type Slot<T> = { promise: Promise<T>; resolve: (value: T) => void };

function deferred<T>(): Slot<T> {
  let resolve!: (value: T) => void;
  const promise = new Promise<T>((res) => {
    resolve = res;
  });
  return { promise, resolve };
}

async function settle(promise: Promise<unknown>, action: () => void) {
  await act(async () => {
    action();
    await promise.catch(() => undefined);
  });
}

const names = (pattern: RegExp) =>
  screen.queryAllByRole("button", { name: pattern }).map((node) => node.textContent);

afterEach(() => {
  vi.useRealTimers();
});

describe("d24_mixed_gauntlet", () => {
  test("ex1 - VoucherBox judges the code, not the typing", () => {
    const onRedeem = vi.fn();
    render(<VoucherBox onRedeem={onRedeem} />);

    const box = screen.getByLabelText("Voucher");
    expect(screen.getByRole("status"), "an empty box has nothing to redeem").toHaveTextContent(
      "Keep typing",
    );
    expect(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Redeem" })).toBeDisabled();

    fireEvent.change(box, { target: { value: "  ab  " } });
    expect(box, "the box shows exactly what was typed, spaces and all").toHaveValue("  ab  ");
    expect(
      screen.getByRole("status"),
      "but the code is what is left after trimming, and two characters is not " +
        "five. Judging the raw string counts the spaces the user cannot see " +
        "(README ex1)",
    ).toHaveTextContent("Keep typing");

    fireEvent.change(box, { target: { value: "  spring20 " } });
    expect(screen.getByRole("status"), "now there is a code").toHaveTextContent("Ready");
    const redeem = screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Redeem" });
    expect(redeem, "and something to press").toBeEnabled();

    fireEvent.click(redeem);
    expect(
      onRedeem,
      "the server wants the code, not the keystrokes - trimmed and upper case",
    ).toHaveBeenLastCalledWith("SPRING20");
  }, 30000);

  test("ex2 - RosterBoard promotes one person at a time", () => {
    const { rerender } = render(<RosterBoard people={["Ada", "Bo", "Cai"]} />);

    expect(names(/^Promote/), "everyone, in the order they came").toEqual([
      "Promote Ada",
      "Promote Bo",
      "Promote Cai",
    ]);
    expect(screen.queryByText("Ada (lead)"), "nobody leads to begin with").toBeNull();

    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Promote Bo" }));
    expect(screen.queryByText("Bo (lead)"), "the promoted person leads").not.toBeNull();
    expect(names(/^Promote/), "and goes to the front").toEqual([
      "Promote Bo",
      "Promote Ada",
      "Promote Cai",
    ]);

    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Promote Cai" }));
    expect(screen.queryByText("Cai (lead)"), "a new lead leads").not.toBeNull();
    expect(
      screen.queryByText("Bo (lead)"),
      "and the old one stops - there is one lead, so it is one piece of state, " +
        "not a flag on every row (README ex2)",
    ).toBeNull();
    expect(
      names(/^Promote/),
      "the new lead is at the front and everybody else is back in the order " +
        "they arrived in",
    ).toEqual(["Promote Cai", "Promote Ada", "Promote Bo"]);

    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Reset" }));
    expect(names(/^Promote/), "reset puts the roster back as it arrived").toEqual([
      "Promote Ada",
      "Promote Bo",
      "Promote Cai",
    ]);
    expect(screen.queryByText("Ada (lead)"), "with nobody leading").toBeNull();

    rerender(<RosterBoard people={[]} />);
    expect(screen.queryByRole("status"), "an empty roster says so").toHaveTextContent(
      "Nobody on the roster",
    );
    expect(screen.queryAllByRole("listitem").length, "and lists nothing").toBe(0);
  }, 30000);

  test("ex3 - IdleWatcher starts counting again every time something happens", () => {
    vi.useFakeTimers();
    const first = vi.fn();
    const second = vi.fn();

    const { rerender, unmount } = render(<IdleWatcher timeoutMs={1000} onIdle={first} />);

    expect(screen.getByRole("status"), "somebody is here").toHaveTextContent("Active");

    act(() => {
      vi.advanceTimersByTime(900);
    });
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Activity" }));
    act(() => {
      vi.advanceTimersByTime(900);
    });
    expect(
      screen.getByRole("status"),
      "1800ms have passed and none of it was quiet for a whole second. An " +
        "effect that starts the countdown once never restarts it, and the page " +
        "logs somebody out while they are typing (README ex3)",
    ).toHaveTextContent("Active");
    expect(first, "so nothing has gone idle").not.toHaveBeenCalled();

    act(() => {
      vi.advanceTimersByTime(200);
    });
    expect(screen.getByRole("status"), "a full second of quiet is idle").toHaveTextContent("Idle");
    expect(first, "reported once").toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);

    act(() => {
      vi.advanceTimersByTime(5000);
    });
    expect(first, "and once only").toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
    expect(vi.getTimerCount(), "with nothing left ticking").toBe(0);

